Subject: Give a generated native entry the light frame it must build itself, and the pieces around it

What this does
  Adds the layout fields a compiled unit's hand-written native entry needs to
  build a callee's light frame on the C stack without calling back into the
  engine, and the four helpers that are more than a plain store: sealing the
  arena over the activation's frame, throwing the interpreter's stack-overflow
  RangeError, releasing a frame's variable area on return, and a check build
  that rebuilds the frame the engine would have built and compares.

Why we need it
  A compiled caller's direct call is a plain C call into the callee's
  speculative body, so the frame that body runs on is the caller's stack
  buffer. That frame has to be the one `regvm_light_fill` builds, field for
  field: every handler, every cold arm and every deopt path reads it, and a
  field the caller forgets is a crash much later rather than an error here.
  Most of it is offsets and plain stores, which the unit does itself, but four
  pieces are not: `regvm_light_seal` and `regvm_light_free` are static engine
  functions, the stack-overflow throw must be the same RangeError the
  interpreter raises, and only the engine can cross-check a hand-built frame
  against the one it would have built.

  Measured cost, from the experiments the call path was designed from: an
  interpreted call is 10.8-11.9 ns, and a framed native call through these
  pieces is 7.0-8.8 ns, against 11.0 ns for the previous call path.

What it adds
  JSAotGenFunc              - `light_var_count`: the variable area's size, from
                              the engine's own promotion-map rule. `light_need`
                              bakes it in without saying whether the area exists,
                              so without this a native entry cannot fill and
                              release exactly the slots the engine does.

  JSAotGenLayout            - off_regrun_ret_ip, _fr, _var_refs, _hdr_pack,
                              _cap_ip, off_fnbc_realm, off_rt_regvm_cur,
                              off_rt_stack_limit, off_object_func_var_refs,
                              light_prefix_slots, regvm_flag_light,
                              _c_entry, _stack, _trivial_ret, _same_realm
  qjs_aot_seal              - raises the arena top over an activation's frame,
                              once, so a callee that allocates lands above it
  qjs_aot_throw_stack_overflow
                            - the interpreter's stack-overflow RangeError, for
                              a native entry that finds the C stack nearly
                              exhausted
  qjs_aot_light_release     - releases the counted values of a native frame's
                              variable area, which is the whole teardown when
                              the frame is the caller's stack buffer
  qjs_aot_frame_check       - check builds only (E2_CHECK): rebuild the frame
                              the engine would have built for this call and
                              abort if a header field differs
  qjs_aot_pic_ensure        - allocate the callee's property-cache table before
                              a native entry publishes its frame. The callee's
                              inline handlers read the table with no NULL test,
                              so it must exist first; allocating is a safepoint,
                              which is exactly why it happens before the frame
                              exists rather than inside a body that has already
                              published one

  JSRuntime                 - `regvm_cur` moves above the `#if QJS_AOT` block.
                              The generator is built with QJS_AOT_GEN but not
                              QJS_AOT, so a field placed after a build-dependent
                              member has one offset in the generator and another
                              in the runtime's own object. The layout hash
                              covers every field, so the two disagreed and the
                              engine refused every unit at bind -- silently,
                              with no diagnostic: `aot: unit=0 bound=0 enter=0`
                              and the whole unit ran interpreted while still
                              producing correct output. The invariant the move
                              states is that every field the unit reads an
                              offset of precedes every `#if` in the struct.

  regvm_s_ROP_get_global    - fills the instruction's PIC site on both the cell
                              hit and the slow path, as the threaded handler
                              does. Without it a compiled body that runs this
                              op as an op call never fills the site, so its
                              inline global-read hit test compares against an
                              empty entry and misses on every execution: a
                              permanent 0% hit rate.

Bytecode version
  No.

